      "title": "Hiding a third label must preserve the pair law",
      "html": "<figure class=\"volume8-explain\" id=\"visual-V56\" data-v8=\"V56\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>V56</span><h3>Hiding a third label must preserve the pair law</h3></header><div class=\"v8-controls\" ><button type=\"button\" data-splitmode=\"balanced\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Balance visible sample</button><button type=\"button\" data-splitmode=\"iid\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Independent fair bits</button></div><div class=\"v8-controls\" data-input-group=\"balanced\"><button type=\"button\" data-splitinput=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Isolate 1</button><button type=\"button\" data-splitinput=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Isolate 2</button><button type=\"button\" data-splitinput=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Isolate 3</button></div><div class=\"v8-controls\" data-input-group=\"iid\" hidden><button type=\"button\" data-splitinput=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\">000</button><button type=\"button\" data-splitinput=\"1\" aria-pressed=\"true\">001</button><button type=\"button\" data-splitinput=\"2\" aria-pressed=\"false\">010</button><button type=\"button\" data-splitinput=\"3\" aria-pressed=\"false\">011</button><button type=\"button\" data-splitinput=\"4\" aria-pressed=\"false\">100</button><button type=\"button\" data-splitinput=\"5\" aria-pressed=\"false\">101</button><button type=\"button\" data-splitinput=\"6\" aria-pressed=\"false\">110</button><button type=\"button\" data-splitinput=\"7\" aria-pressed=\"false\">111</button></div><picture data-v8-picture><source media=\"(max-width:700px)\" srcset=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-volume8-v1/V56-en-balanced-2-mobile.svg\"><img class=\"v8-scene\" src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-volume8-v1/V56-en-balanced-2-desktop.svg\" alt=\"Hiding a third label must preserve the pair law\"></picture><div class=\"v8-print\"><section><h4>Hiding a third label must preserve the pair law · 1/2</h4><img src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-volume8-v1/V56.en.page1.svg\" alt=\"Hiding a third label must preserve the pair law\"><p>Only the finite generator of one block is compared, with raw candidate-event rate 1. Balancing the observed sample always separates two labels; among the three equiprobable singleton sides for three labels, a fixed pair separates with probability 2/3. In the independent fair-bit model the pair separates with probability 1/2 both directly and after restricting three labels. The eight bit words are equiprobable; 000 and 111 cause no effective split. Hiding label 3 removes an observation, not the colors of labels 1 and 2. Visible rates are raw rate times separation probability. General infinite fragmentation, independent block futures and integrability still require the text.</p></section><section><h4>Hiding a third label must preserve the pair law · 2/2</h4><img src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-volume8-v1/V56.en.page2.svg\" alt=\"Hiding a third label must preserve the pair law\"><p>Only the finite generator of one block is compared, with raw candidate-event rate 1. Balancing the observed sample always separates two labels; among the three equiprobable singleton sides for three labels, a fixed pair separates with probability 2/3. In the independent fair-bit model the pair separates with probability 1/2 both directly and after restricting three labels. The eight bit words are equiprobable; 000 and 111 cause no effective split. Hiding label 3 removes an observation, not the colors of labels 1 and 2. Visible rates are raw rate times separation probability. General infinite fragmentation, independent block futures and integrability still require the text.</p></section></div><output data-v8-result aria-live=\"polite\">First test sample balancing: direct rate 1, restricted rate 2/3—inconsistent. Switch to independent bits: both rates are 1/2.</output><details><summary>Conditions, calculations and limits</summary><p>Only the finite generator of one block is compared, with raw candidate-event rate 1. Balancing the observed sample always separates two labels; among the three equiprobable singleton sides for three labels, a fixed pair separates with probability 2/3. In the independent fair-bit model the pair separates with probability 1/2 both directly and after restricting three labels. The eight bit words are equiprobable; 000 and 111 cause no effective split. Hiding label 3 removes an observation, not the colors of labels 1 and 2. Visible rates are raw rate times separation probability. General infinite fragmentation, independent block futures and integrability still require the text.</p><p><a href=\"/chapters/56-fragmentation-hierarchies.html\">Book §56.1, §56.8–9; finite generator check</a></p></details><figcaption>Exact finite models or deterministic constructions; diagrams do not replace proofs.</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-volume8-v1/V56.en.svg\">SVG</a><a href=\"/print/figures/V56.en.html\">Static print</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "Only the finite generator of one block is compared, with raw candidate-event rate 1. Balancing the observed sample always separates two labels; among the three equiprobable singleton sides for three labels, a fixed pair separates with probability 2/3. In the independent fair-bit model the pair separates with probability 1/2 both directly and after restricting three labels. The eight bit words are equiprobable; 000 and 111 cause no effective split. Hiding label 3 removes an observation, not the colors of labels 1 and 2. Visible rates are raw rate times separation probability. General infinite fragmentation, independent block futures and integrability still require the text.",
